{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"presheaves-monadic-comonadic-over-families","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Presheaves are monadic and comonadic over families"}]},"title_text":"Presheaves are monadic and comonadic over families","kind":"theorem","taxon":null,"url":"presheaves-monadic-comonadic-over-families.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","presheaves-monadic-comonadic-over-families"],["kind","theorem"],["label","Theorem"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"presheaf-family-adjoint-triple","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"adjoint triple"}]}},{"Text":" "},{"Math":{"src":"\"Free\" ⊣ U ⊣ \"Cofree\""}},{"Text":" induces a monad "},{"Math":{"src":"T = U ∘ \"Free\""}},{"Text":" and a comonad "},{"Math":{"src":"W = U ∘ \"Cofree\""}},{"Text":" on "},{"Math":{"src":"\"Fam\" lr(( cal(C) ))"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Both "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"comparison-functor","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"comparison functors"}]}},{"Text":" are equivalences: presheaves are the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"eilenberg-moore-displayed","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"Eilenberg–Moore algebras"}]}},{"Text":" of "},{"Math":{"src":"T"}},{"Text":" and the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"co-eilenberg-moore-displayed","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"co-Eilenberg–Moore coalgebras"}]}},{"Text":" of "},{"Math":{"src":"W"}},{"Text":","}]},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"Psh\") thin cal(C) ≃ \"EM\" lr(( T )) wide sans(\"Psh\") thin cal(C) ≃ \"coEM\" lr(( W )) ."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"So presheaves are both "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"monadicity-comonadicity","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"monadic and comonadic"}]}},{"Text":" over families."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Reading the algebra structure concretely: a "},{"Math":{"src":"T"}},{"Text":"-algebra on a family "},{"Math":{"src":"A"}},{"Text":" is a map "},{"Math":{"src":"∑_y cal(C) lr(( x \\, y )) × A lr(( y )) -> A lr(( x ))"}},{"Text":" for each "},{"Math":{"src":"x"}},{"Text":", subject to the monad algebra laws — that is, exactly a functorial action of restriction."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The comonadic reading is the same structure seen from the element’s side: a "},{"Math":{"src":"W"}},{"Text":"-coalgebra is a map "},{"Math":{"src":"A lr(( x )) -> ∏_y cal(C) lr(( y \\, x )) -> A lr(( y ))"}},{"Text":", giving each value its restriction along every morphism into "},{"Math":{"src":"x"}},{"Text":". Where the monad says restriction "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"acts on"}]},{"Text":" values, the comonad says a value "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"already carries"}]},{"Text":" all of its restrictions — and the coalgebra laws say it does so coherently."}]}]}}}]}}
